# "Use Table AI to format" → canonical instruction

When the user asks to format anything with the **Table AI** brand, use the
vendored brand tokens below via the `docx-master` pipeline. Do not re-derive
colors/fonts from scratch — they are already mapped from the source design.

## Brand source of truth

- **Brand module (use this):** `modules/tableai-brand/design.md`
- **Authoritative design source:** `/Users/af/cpro01/prioritized01/00tableai3/000tableai_designaha001/TABLEAI/TableAI_DESIGN.md`
- **Upstream repo:** https://github.com/fengurt/tableai_designaha/tree/main/TABLEAI
- **Tokens:** 寰宇深蓝 (Universe Deep Blue) `#0A1626` (primary ink/structure) ·
  日晷暗金 (Sundial Dark Gold) `#A88B52` (accent: key data, CTAs, heading rules only) ·
  白底 `#FFFFFF` · Manrope (Latin) / Noto Sans SC (CJK) · investor-grade minimal, generous whitespace.
- **Voice / 4AATE:** Altruistic, Authentic, Artistic, Elegant.

## Default build (Word / .docx)

```bash
pnpm docx:from-md:build -- \
  --md out/<slug>.md \
  --brand modules/tableai-brand/design.md \
  --slug <slug> --client "<client>" --tag "<tags>"
```

- Save the source content verbatim to `out/<slug>.md` first — **never drop content**.
- Output lands in `out/documents/<slug>/` (docx + pdf + preview PNGs + meta.json),
  which surfaces in the html-lab Documents library (`pnpm dev:html-lab`).
- Verify by reading the preview PNGs before reporting done.

## Future online deployment

The brand is self-contained in `modules/tableai-brand/design.md` (tokens baked in,
no external fetch needed at build time), so it is safe to bundle for hosted/online
docx generation. If the upstream `TableAI_DESIGN.md` changes, re-map tokens into the
brand module and keep the `source:` pointer in its frontmatter up to date.

## Other surfaces

For HTML / PPTX / web UI branded as Table AI, apply the same tokens (deep blue
structure, gold accent only on key data & CTAs, white background, 8px spacing grid,
2–4px or square corners).
